{
  "dom_id": "step-e4745",
  "name": "Example: Problem Solving Using the Ratio of Two Integers",
  "problem": "If a machine at a factory takes $6$ hours to complete $2$ batches of refractory bricks, how many hours does it take to complete $10$ batches?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the number of hours it takes the machine to complete $10$ batches of refractory bricks, we first find the unit rate of hours per batch and then multiply the unit rate by $10$ batches.\n\nTo find the unit rate of hours per batch, we divide the number of hours, $6,$ by the number of batches, $2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6÷2 & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $3$ hours per batch. To find the number of hours it takes the machine to complete $10$ batches, we multiply the unit rate by $10$ batches and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\times 10 & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the machine $30$ hours to complete $10$ batches.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
